---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Contribute"
  description="Contribute code, receiver validation, documentation or signature evidence to AirHound."
>
  <header class="page-header wrap">
    <h1>
      Bring evidence.
      <br />
      Build together.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A reproducible observation, a clearer guide or a well-tested fix can all
      move the project forward.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap content prose">
    <ul class="toc-list">
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/reference/contributing/">
            Contribute code or documentation
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Start with the repository contribution guide, check the{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/issues/160">roadmap</a>,
          and run the relevant{" "}
          <a href="/reference/docs/testing/">tests and quality checks</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/reference/docs/signature-packs/">Propose a signature</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Provide source/provenance, reuse terms, exact matching fields,
          device/model/state evidence and ordinary-device negative fixtures.
          Review{" "}
          <a href="/reference/docs/signature-research/">existing research</a>{" "}
          before adding a candidate.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/reference/docs/receiver-release-gates/">
            Validate a receiver
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Record exact hardware, firmware, operating system and test conditions.
          Distinguish parser replay from live RF reception; keep raw identifying
          captures private.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/issues">
            Report a problem
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Search existing issues, then include component/revision, expected and
          observed behavior, and sanitized steps to reproduce. Do not post real
          nearby MACs, SSIDs or GPS locations.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Security reports</h2>
    <p>
      Private vulnerability reporting availability is a maintainer decision.
      Check{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/security">
        the repository Security page
      </a>{" "}
      for the currently available reporting route. Do not publish sensitive
      exploit details or private captures in a public issue.
    </p>
    <h2>Component boundaries matter</h2>
    <p>
      The shared project is MIT licensed. The independent MT7610U receiver is
      GPL-2.0-only; the Sniffle source helper is GPL-3.0-only. Keep notices and
      corresponding-source requirements with each component.{" "}
      <a href="/privacy/#licenses">Review the license links.</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Site>
